In a glob view an empty file of every supported extension has nothing to summarize, so each
prints `(0 lines): (no header available)`.
== args
input
== file input/empty.md
== file input/empty.ts
== file input/empty.tsx
== file input/empty.js
== file input/empty.rs
== file input/empty.css
== file input/empty.json
== file input/empty.toml
== file input/empty.yaml
== stdout
glob view: input
input/empty.css (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.js (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.json (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.md (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.rs (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.toml (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.ts (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.tsx (0 lines): (no header available)
input/empty.yaml (0 lines): (no header available)
== stderr
== exit 0
